From: ScorchDroid <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: bitmap rows bottom-up, as every other loader's are

The port's own ImageBitmapFactory (patch 0005, replacing the SDL one)
turned a BMP's rows over on the way in. A BMP is stored bottom-up, and
the Image convention - upstream's SDL path, the JPEG and PNG loaders,
and what glTexImage2D expects - is bottom-up too, so the flip left
every .bmp texture upside down: tank and ship skins sampled the wrong
half of their image (a grey destroyer drew in its hull's navy), the
tree needle masks, the breaker crescents and the speech bubble were
inverted. Rows now land in file order; a top-down file (negative
height) is the one that gets turned over.

---
diff --git a/src/common/image/ImageBitmapFactory.cpp b/src/common/image/ImageBitmapFactory.cpp
--- a/src/common/image/ImageBitmapFactory.cpp
+++ b/src/common/image/ImageBitmapFactory.cpp
@@ -95,7 +95,12 @@
 			return Image();
 		}
 
-		int destRowIndex = topDown ? row : (result.getHeight() - row - 1);
+		// Image rows run bottom-up, the way every other loader here and
+		// upstream's SDL_LoadBMP path leave them (row 0 is the bottom of
+		// the picture, which is also what glTexImage2D expects). A BMP
+		// file is stored bottom-up too, so its rows land in file order;
+		// only a top-down file (negative height) is turned over.
+		int destRowIndex = topDown ? (result.getHeight() - row - 1) : row;
 		unsigned char *destRow = result.getBits() + (destRowIndex * (result.getWidth() * result.getComponents()));
 		unsigned char *from = rowBuffer.data();
 		for (int j = 0; j < result.getWidth(); j++)
